From: Ivan Semenov <ivan@ray.app>
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: dt-platdev: allow Siflower SF19A2890

The SF19A2890 CPU clock is a plain mux/divider handled by the SoC
clock driver and the cpu nodes carry an operating-points table, so
the generic cpufreq-dt driver works as-is (the stock firmware uses
exactly this setup). Add the SoC to the allowlist so the platform
device gets created.

Signed-off-by: Ivan Semenov <ivan@ray.app>
---
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -178,6 +178,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id blockli
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650", },
 
+	{ .compatible = "siflower,sf19a2890", },
+
 	{ .compatible = "st,stih407", },
 	{ .compatible = "st,stih410", },
 	{ .compatible = "st,stih418", },
